From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruskin Constant <ruskin@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:25:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Allow path() for shape-outside

shape-outside's AllowedBasicShapes::SHAPE_OUTSIDE bitset predates
path() joining <basic-shape> and never got the PATH bit, even though
Path and FillRule parsing is already complete and unconditionally
compiled (shared with clip-path, which allows it). shape() stays
excluded because it has its own pref gate. shape-outside has no
downstream layout consumer for any basic-shape kind, so this is
grammar completion only.
---
 values/specified/basic_shape.rs | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/values/specified/basic_shape.rs b/values/specified/basic_shape.rs
index bdedc60..17ce546 100644
--- a/values/specified/basic_shape.rs
+++ b/values/specified/basic_shape.rs
@@ -187,13 +187,17 @@ bitflags! {
             Self::PATH.bits() |
             Self::SHAPE.bits();

-        /// For shape-outside.
+        /// For shape-outside. path() shares Path/FillRule with clip-path
+        /// (see ALL above) and has no shape-outside-specific handling, so
+        /// it's safe to allow here too. shape() stays excluded because
+        /// it is gated on its own pref.
         const SHAPE_OUTSIDE =
             Self::INSET.bits() |
             Self::XYWH.bits() |
             Self::RECT.bits() |
             Self::CIRCLE.bits() |
             Self::ELLIPSE.bits() |
-            Self::POLYGON.bits();
+            Self::POLYGON.bits() |
+            Self::PATH.bits();
     }
 }
